SM(194,{"n":"Ephesians 3.1-10","a":"Fr Stephen De Young Archives/Ephesians 3.1-10.mp3","d":3030.6,"s":[[0.3,"So we'll go ahead and uh get started."],[4.54,"And uh when we get started in just a moment, we're gonna be picking up uh at the beginning of uh St."],[13.82,"Paul's Epistle to the Ephesians, uh, chapter 3."],[19.1,"Unless someone tells me I'm wrong."],[21.58,"But I don't think so."],[23.66,"So um but to uh do our sort of quick catch up, um we're not super far into St."],[33.42,"Paul's Epistle to the Ephesians, but just to quickly, we call it St."],[36.62,"Paul's Epistle to the Ephesians, but it was actually probably written from Ephesus, not to Ephesus, although it circulated in Ephesus in the area around Ephesus uh in uh Asia Minor, uh, what's now Turkey."],[51.58,"Um as we've been uh going through the first couple of chapters, St."],[62.18,"Paul in the first chapter we saw was really laying out what we as Orthodox Christians call theosis about the destiny of humans to become be adopted as sons of God and to share in God's eternal divine life."],[82.82,"And he right at the end of chapter two sort of segued from that because he's been talking about the renewal of humanity in Christ."],[93.94,"So that allowed him to segue into the unity of Jews and Gentiles in Christ, because whether you were a pagan or whether you were a Judean or Jewish before coming to Christ, now that you've come to Christ, you are a new creation and have that same new humanity."],[121.38,"He ended chapter 2 by using the metaphor of a temple that's being built with a foundation laid by the apostles and prophets, Christ, the chief cornerstone, and them as sort of living bricks being built into this, together into this temple, this place where God dwells among them."],[145.3,"So that may be the quickest recap I've ever done."],[148.66,"But that's fine."],[149.7,"We'll go ahead."],[151.02,"And unless anybody has any questions or comments or uh really late election results, we'll start in uh St."],[161.14,"Paul's Epistle of Ephesians, chapter 3, verse 1."],[162.34,"Okay. Did you have a late return?"],[171.1,"So chapter 3, verse 1."],[174.06,"For this reason, I, Paul, the prisoner of Christ Jesus, for you Gentiles."],[179.82,"If indeed you have heard of the dispensation of the grace of God, which was given to me for you."],[186.38,"We'll pause there, because this is one of St."],[188.7,"Paul's very, very long sentences."],[193.42,"Even in English."],[194.46,"You can tell it's truly, it's truly a St."],[197.58,"Paul Greek sentence when they can't even figure out where to break it up in English."],[203.66,"Because it's gotten so nested and uh and complex."],[208.54,"Um but so he begins for this reason."],[213.74,"For this reason, everything he's just described that we just very quickly recapped."],[220.3,"He's Paul, and he is uh the prisoner of Christ Jesus for you for you of the nations, for you former pagans."],[230.06,"Is prisoner there literal or prisoner prisoner here is literal."],[235.18,"This is a point where he was spending time in jail."],[240.14,"That's um, and we saw how his time in Ephesus was somewhat troubled uh in uh the Acts of the Apostles."],[249.5,"Um so this is a period where he has been in prison."],[252.22,"He was in prison many times, as we saw."],[254.94,"Um, but uh yeah, this is one of them."],[259.74,"Um, but he's he's um you know, of we've talked before that um when you have Bible translations done by committees, and there are translations where there's some nuance, and you've got a committee, they tend to like to punt and kind of give sort of the most bare bones non-committal."],[285.3,"So prisoner of Christ Jesus is that kind of thing."],[289.22,"That makes it sound like Christ has him in a cage or something."],[294.18,"Yeah. And that's that could also just mean for."],[300.66,"Yeah. Right? Or that thing?"],[304.5,"When they tried to just say English, was that an English word?"],[307.86,"Yeah. Yeah, it's just there, yeah."],[310.74,"It's it's just there is no there is no actual preposition there in Greek."],[317.78,"It's just a Greek genitive."],[320.18,"Okay. And you can interpret genitives in various ways."],[326.1,"Um, and so it's a way of relating it to, so he's a prisoner related to Christ Jesus, but how that there's nuance there."],[338.98,"And so uh the idea there is that St."],[344.66,"Paul is trying to convey that he's not a prisoner of the people who actually imprisoned him."],[355.86,"Right? That's not why he's sitting in prison."],[359.14,"He didn't commit a crime."],[362.34,"He's not complaining about being persecuted."],[367.06,"He's he's saying, he gives two reasons here why he's in prison."],[372.46,"Number one, he's in prison for Christ."],[378.06,"Right? He belongs to Christ, and that's why he's in prison, and then also for the sake of the Gentiles."],[386.54,"Right? For these former pagans who have now become Christians, who have now entered uh the church."],[395.9,"And that's why he begins verse 2 with if indeed you have heard of the dispensation of the grace of God, which is given to me for you."],[404.06,"Okay, so if he's the one who preached the grace of God, which is what he was just describing, remember in the last two chapters."],[413.42,"He was describing the gift, the gift of salvation, the gift of adoption and sonship."],[421.34,"That dispensation of the grace of God."],[423.1,"He said, if you heard about it from me."],[426.46,"So what does that mean?"],[427.58,"When he says he's a prisoner there for their sake, it's I'm locked up because I came preaching this for you."],[436.3,"Okay. Right. So he's out promoting the cause of Christ, and he's out proclaiming this gift of grace, right, to these former pagans."],[451.5,"That's why he's locked up in prison."],[454.14,"Okay, that's what he's been doing."],[455.9,"Not he committed an actual crime."],[460.22,"Or you know, the governor hates him personally, or anything like that."],[464.38,"These are the reasons."],[465.34,"So he said he he he wants them to know that he's in prison because of what he was doing for them in the cause of Christ."],[477.7,"So verse 3 how that by revelation he made known to me the mystery, as I have briefly written already, by which when you read you may understand my knowledge in the mystery of Christ."],[490.34,"So now that how there means he's now going into more detail on the dispensation of the grace of God that was given to him."],[501.46,"So he says, There's this dispensation of the grace of God that I preach to you that was given to Saint Paul, and now he's saying, Here's what more unpacking what that is."],[513.3,"Here's what I mean by that."],[514.58,"And he says he's briefly written already."],[516.74,"Does that refer to a previous letter that we don't have or something like that?"],[521.14,"It's somewhat ambiguous."],[524.66,"It could be another letter."],[526.18,"He could just be referring to the last couple chapters."],[529.14,"Oh. Um, yeah, it's it's a little ambiguous."],[538.02,"It just says that he's written about it previously."],[542.1,"Well, that could mean what we've just read, right, which would fit."],[546.74,"Uh-huh. Uh, or it could mean that there was another communication."],[555.06,"And so um, by revelation he made known to me the myth."],[559.46,"So Christ revealed himself to St."],[564.02,"Paul, right, on the road to Damascus, and made known to him the mystery."],[573.22,"Okay. Um that he says he has written about already, and by which, when you read, you may understand his knowledge in his his knowledge related to the mystery of Christ."],[590.06,"Okay. So Christ appears to Saint Paul, he gives him the knowledge of this mystery, and Saint Paul has conveyed that to them."],[604.22,"So what's up with this word mystery?"],[607.18,"Is it related to the mystery holes sometime or well the term is."],[611.58,"Yeah, the term is."],[613.66,"Yeah, this isn't mystery like who done it."],[618.62,"Like and it's not, it's not mystery in sort of the purely esoteric sense."],[628.14,"Okay. Um we tend to, as modern people, understand the word mystery as, well, this is just a piece of knowledge."],[640.78,"Knowledge of the mystery, this is some secret."],[644.3,"Right? It's some fact or information or knowledge that's been kept secret, but that was conveyed to St."],[652.54,"Paul, and he's now conveyed it to them."],[655.9,"But that's not what mystery meant to someone in Ephesus in the first century AD."],[663.74,"When we talk about mystery religions and mystery cults."],[667.02,"We talked about this a little bit in the introductions, an introduction to 1 Corinthians, because of the mysteries of Demeter in Corinth."],[677.38,"These mysteries, it wasn't that, you know, it wasn't like Scientology, where they bring you in, and once you reach a certain level, they tell you about the Dark Lord Zenu and the aliens and the volcanoes."],[691.62,"That's that's not how it worked."],[693.7,"Yeah. It wasn't sort of this secret stuff that they don't tell everybody."],[699.06,"That they only tell you, it's not like the Freemasons."],[702.66,"Um the the mystery cults and mystery religions were related to what made them a mystery cult or a mystery religion, as opposed to just a regular old pagan cult."],[717.38,"Or pagan religion, was that they had rites of initiation."],[724.34,"They had rites of initiation."],[726.74,"And those rites of initiation, again, were not being you having factual information revealed to you."],[734.42,"They were uh putting people through sort of extreme experiences."],[741.14,"Like kind of like uh when you're uh like being hazed on the way to a fraternity?"],[746.42,"Yeah. Yeah. Much more extreme."],[748.66,"On a much more kind of extreme level, and not just you're joining a club, but this was thought most of them involved some kind of experience of death, of near death, or death, or entering the realm of the dead."],[766.34,"Or experiencing some kind of spiritual death and rebirth."],[771.14,"These kind of ideas."],[779.94,"Yeah, death. Persephone."],[782.38,"Um, percent. Yeah."],[783.34,"Yeah. And so, for example, uh people would be put in darkness and taken to sort of the edges of pits and cliffs and that kind of thing, or to experience falling."],[797.02,"Some of them they would uh put someone under a grate in darkness and then kill a bull and dump its blood all over them."],[806.38,"Um these extreme, sometimes they would use uh what we would now call psychedelic drugs, right, to sort of induce these sort of extreme experiences."],[817.66,"And so that once someone had gone through it, right, they would they would have had this experience which they identified as a religious experience."],[827.9,"Of death and rebirth that they would believe would then give them some kind of perspective or understanding on the world that they didn't have before."],[837.9,"I thought most of those mystery calls promised uh eternal life."],[843.1,"Well, eventually down the road, yeah."],[845.82,"That's yeah. Um we talked about we talked about in uh chapter two."],[853.82,"And that's where we're going with this."],[855.82,"Chapter two, remember, uh St."],[858.22,"Paul's talking about deification, he's talking about theosis."],[861.82,"And he made the point that this isn't sort of like apotheosis in in pagan traditions where you perform some mighty deeds, right, or something that impress the gods."],[873.82,"And so you end up exalted, right, into this state."],[879.1,"That that's not how it works."],[880.94,"That's not how adoption is sons of God works."],[883.66,"Um, and so there's a similar kind of idea at work here when he's talking about the mysteries of Christ."],[890.1,"Right? St. Paul is talking about having an experience."],[893.58,"He's talking about an experience he had on the road to Damascus."],[896.78,"When Christ revealed himself to him."],[896.94,"But note that Christ revealed himself to him."],[903.3,"Christ didn't show up and tell him some arcane secrets."],[908.82,"Right? He didn't tell him the secret name of God that he could pronounce and make magic things happen."],[914.74,"Right? He didn't tell him the keywords to get past the gatekeepers to the afterlife."],[920.66,"Like in Isis cults."],[922.9,"He didn't he didn't convey anything."],[925.38,"He revealed himself to him."],[928.66,"Right. And so for Saint Paul, it's Christ Himself who is the mystery."],[937.46,"Right? Christ Himself who is the mystery."],[939.54,"And this is related to the idea in St."],[943.14,"John's Gospel of Christ as the logos."],[947.46,"Right? As being sort of the reason behind creation."],[951.62,"Right? So for St."],[952.9,"Paul, once you encounter Christ, once you come to know Christ, once you're in Christ."],[959.3,"Now you can look out and make sense of the world and understand it."],[965.3,"And ultimately receive adoption and eternal life."],[969.7,"Right? But it's not through an esoteric experience that you would go and chase after."],[975.06,"By making a pilgrimage and going through these rituals, but it's by coming to know Christ."],[980.5,"And it's not an experience that's imposed on you by another person."],[985.22,"Right. Right. There's no application of a technique."],[990.18,"That produces this or magic."],[993.06,"There's no smoke and mirrors."],[995.22,"There's no chemicals necessary."],[998.18,"There's no bold death necessary."],[1001.14,"There's no. Um yeah, so for Saint Paul, Christ reveals himself to him, and Saint Paul then comes and reveals Christ to the Gentile pagans at Ephesus."],[1022.62,"And so this now gives them not just the adoption he was talking about."],[1029.1,"But also now gives them the means to understand the world, their life, the cosmos."],[1036.78,"They don't need to go and search after some other cosmic mysteries."],[1043.34,"This is kind of a provocative question, I guess."],[1047.1,"Okay. But um if St."],[1051.5,"Paul has a direct experience of Christ, then he tells other people how can his words be the equivalent of this direct experience."],[1064.46,"How do they, how does their hearing what he has to say do the same thing as that direct experience?"],[1072.78,"Well, this is this isn't well because they now, as Saint Paul has been saying, they now are in Christ."],[1082.94,"Because of their baptism, right, because of the because of their baptism."],[1085.9,"So they have now had this, they've now come to know Christ themselves."],[1090.7,"They haven't just heard about Christ."],[1093.26,"They've now come to know Christ themselves through Saint Paul's preaching."],[1099.26,"But Saint Paul is using the wording he's using not only because these are former pagans and this is how they understand religion, but also that this isn't like a philosophical system or a self-help system."],[1112.18,"It's not like stoicism, like here's here's how you should practice to have a happy and successful life, you know."],[1118.98,"And and right, it's not a philosophy, it's not right, it's coming to know Christ Himself."],[1125.38,"Christ Himself does this."],[1128.42,"Which was his big focus in chapter one and chapter two, that's the grace of God."],[1133.3,"Christ does this."],[1137.22,"For them to have their own direct experience."],[1141.14,"It's a mean by means by which St."],[1143.86,"Paul's proclamation of the gospel is a means by which Christ chooses to reveal himself."],[1149.54,"Okay. Right? He doesn't have to."],[1156.82,"It's not his preaching that does it."],[1158.98,"His preaching is the means for Christ."],[1161.86,"The means that Christ."],[1163.46,"Right. And it's it's this is related to what we've talked about about prayer."],[1169.62,"Right? And how prayer works."],[1172.02,"Prayer isn't magic where it makes God do something."],[1175.62,"Right? If we just get enough people or the right people or whatever, then God will do what we want if we all pray."],[1181.62,"That's not how it works."],[1182.9,"But God chooses to work through the prayers of the saints, the prayers of his people."],[1188.26,"And so we offer our prayers to God."],[1191.78,"For him to, when he chooses, do that."],[1194.18,"Same thing with Saint Paul."],[1196.18,"Because St. Paul went and preached the gospel a lot of places."],[1198.74,"Not everybody had a direct experience of Christ."],[1202.82,"Right? A lot of people laughed at him, a lot of people, some people threw him in jail."],[1207.78,"So not everyone had that same experience."],[1211.54,"Even the people who met Christ in person didn't all meet Christ in person."],[1216.46,"Right. In this sense that St."],[1218.06,"Paul's talking about it."],[1220.14,"So yeah, it's not magic."],[1222.86,"Right? It's but it's the means by which St."],[1227.58,"Paul has been called."],[1228.62,"And he's going to continue to talk about this as we go forward in this chapter."],[1231.5,"It's the means by which St."],[1233.1,"Paul has been called to bring Christ to now the pagan nations."],[1238.62,"So St. Paul is over here."],[1240.14,"Right. It's through his through his proclamation."],[1242.38,"Yeah, his life is sort of a prayer."],[1244.62,"Yeah. That he's offered to God to use."],[1249.9,"As God sees fit."],[1251.98,"Right. Not as Paul sees fit."],[1256.3,"So verse 5, which in other ages was not made known to the sons of men, as it has now been revealed by the Spirit to his holy apostles and prophets."],[1278.62,"Right? This isn't sort of content."],[1281.5,"This isn't like theology book content."],[1284.78,"Right? They had no idea who Jesus was back then."],[1288.22,"We we see the opposite, like all through the Gospels."],[1290.46,"Christ says Abraham rejoiced to see one of my days."],[1293.98,"He's on Mount Tabor at the Transfiguration talking to Moses and Elijah."],[1298.46,"Moses and Elijah weren't like, who are you?"],[1300.38,"What's this all about?"],[1301.66,"Right? Because Moses had talked to him on a mountain before."],[1306.54,"Back in in uh Sinai."],[1309.58,"Um. But Christ himself, right, was not made known to everybody."],[1321.06,"Right? The average Israelite never had a direct encounter with God."],[1329.06,"Didn't speak to him face to face."],[1332.34,"Right? Didn't didn't know him in that way."],[1335.62,"Now, as St."],[1336.34,"Paul says, the prophets did, Moses did, Elijah did, Isaiah did, Jeremiah did."],[1341.7,"We read about it in the Old Testament."],[1343.7,"Abraham did. But your average Israelite did not."],[1349.94,"But now. Through the Spirit, he has been."],[1357.3,"Right? He has been."],[1358.9,"And so this is St."],[1361.38,"Paul's talking about the transition that happens."],[1366.02,"Right? After Christ's death, resurrection, ascension, Pentecost, the Holy Spirit comes upon all flesh."],[1374.1,"Right? The Holy Spirit's around."],[1376.1,"Spirit of God is around in the Old Testament."],[1378.98,"Right? Spirit comes upon David."],[1381.62,"Spirit comes upon Moses."],[1384.1,"Spirit comes upon the prophets."],[1386.34,"Right? But your average Israelite, no."],[1390.9,"Right? And even when we read about the Holy Spirit coming upon one of these sort of people who God has called to this role of prophet or leader, a lot of times it's not permanent."],[1402.82,"The Holy Spirit comes upon Saul, Saul sins, Holy Spirit leaves."],[1409.3,"Right? The book of the Judges, you know, the same judge will have the Holy Spirit sort of fall on him and possess him for a period of time to do something and then leave again."],[1420.98,"And so there's been this shift now."],[1421.22,"Right? Right. And St."],[1426.86,"Paul's pointing to this, that now what was the province of sort of these few chosen people who had these special roles in the old covenant in ages past."],[1439.1,"In the past age."],[1440.7,"Now in this age is the province of everyone."],[1445.1,"Right? Including these former pagan Gentiles who have received the Holy Spirit."],[1450.54,"And God has done this through the apostles, including Saint Paul."],[1456.86,"Because remember, the Holy Spirit at Pentecost comes first upon the apostles."],[1460.78,"They go out and proclaim the gospel."],[1463.82,"People hear the gospel, are baptized and receive the Holy Spirit."],[1468.14,"Right? So it's through the apostles that God has chosen to do this."],[1473.34,"Right, as St."],[1475.02,"Paul is writing, and this transition has taken place."],[1480.14,"Verse 6. So that the Gentiles should be fellow heirs of the same body and partakers of his promise in Christ through the gospel."],[1495.66,"So that all the pagan nations should be fellow heirs, along with Israel."],[1499.82,"Right? Along with uh, or rather, along with Judea, with Judah, of the same body, partakers of that same promise in Christ through the gospel."],[1511.98,"So that's the goal."],[1513.26,"That's why they've been sent out to call everybody back in."],[1517.14,"Right? They didn't have access to direct this direct access to Christ before."],[1524.1,"Right? And that's St."],[1525.9,"Paul's mission. Yeah."],[1529.3,"Verse 7, of which, this being the gospel."],[1534.1,"Yeah. Oh, yeah."],[1535.38,"I don't think we've had a sentence break yet in this chapter."],[1539.62,"Even in English."],[1543.06,"Of which, meaning of the gospel, I became a minister according to the gift of the grace of God given to me by the effective working of his power."],[1554.42,"So St. Paul became a minister of the gospel to do this."],[1558.1,"He's one of the apostles."],[1560.5,"Who's been called to do this according to the gift of the grace of God given to me?"],[1564.9,"It was God's action."],[1565.86,"God took him and made him an apostle and sent him to do this by the effective working of his power."],[1572.82,"Right? So again, this isn't something St."],[1575.7,"Paul attained. Right."],[1579.7,"He didn't go and meditate."],[1581.46,"He wasn't initiated into some mystery."],[1584.18,"He didn't go to Jerusalem and get initiated by the other apostles into the mysteries."],[1588.9,"And now he's come to them to bring them."],[1590.9,"Right? Right? It's God grabbed him on the road to Damascus."],[1596.98,"Christ revealed himself to him, sent him to do this."],[1600.74,"And now St."],[1601.46,"Paul's doing it."],[1602.66,"And he's wanting to emphasize here that actually, really, you know, Saint Paul's there doing it, but it's really God doing these things for the people he's writing to through Saint Paul."],[1613.78,"So he wants to be clear that it is God doing it through him."],[1617.62,"Right? But it's also God doing it through him."],[1628.58,"Verse 8. New sentence in English."],[1633.66,"To me, who am less than the least of all the saints, this grace was given that I should preach among the Gentiles, among the nations, the unsearchable riches of Christ."],[1649.02,"So he says that he's, you know, the least of everyone who's received these promises."],[1656.38,"That's the saints, the holy ones."],[1657.98,"The sons of God."],[1659.02,"He's the least of them."],[1660.86,"Right? But but despite him being the least, less than the least, God gave him this gift that he would that he would preach to all the nations, nations, the unsearchable riches of Christ."],[1676.86,"Verse 9, and to make all see what is the fellowship of the mystery, which from the beginning of the ages has been hidden in God, who created all things through Jesus Christ."],[1688.86,"Okay. So he's now."],[1693.98,"Again, this isn't a mystery that's still hidden somewhere that you have to go through this, that, and the other, right, to have revealed to you, ritually or otherwise."],[1704.14,"But Saint Paul is now proclaiming it to everyone."],[1709.34,"Right? Proclaiming it to everyone."],[1712.14,"Christ. Right? And he's saying, Christ was hidden in the past."],[1721.5,"Even though he's the one through whom God the Father created everything."],[1727.66,"So he didn't just appear or come into being."],[1732.38,"Recently. Right? He's been around the whole time."],[1736.38,"He's just revealed himself to everyone recently."],[1741.38,"Right? St. Paul isn't saying he's already said the prophets knew him."],[1746.1,"So he's not saying nobody knew anything about him."],[1751.3,"Right? But he wasn't known to everyone."],[1754.58,"Was it known to everyone, including just the pagan nations out there are now hearing who he is through the through the apostles."],[1766.34,"To the intent that now the manifold wisdom of God might be made known by the church to the principalities and powers in the heavenly places according to the eternal purpose which he accomplished in Christ Jesus our Lord."],[1783.54,"So a furrowed brow."],[1789.14,"So I just sort it out."],[1793.22,"What St. Paul is saying here."],[1796.66,"Well, we'll start with who's he talking about?"],[1799.62,"The powers of principalities in the heavenly places."],[1809.38,"Powers of principalities."],[1811.3,"These are we, you know, we do not battle against flesh and blood, but against powers and principalities in the heavenly places."],[1817.3,"We'll get there."],[1822.58,"Right. No. No."],[1824.1,"No. You're operating under the assumption that these folks were all thrown out of the heavenly places."],[1832.58,"But that's not how St."],[1834.02,"Paul talks about it."],[1836.1,"Right? Okay. Because he's going to talk about our war being with powers and principalities in the heavenly places."],[1844.78,"Right? Um so there's a helpful there's a helpful reference about this in uh St."],[1854.14,"Gregory the Dealogist in his Morelia, which is his commentary on the book of Job, he talks about the scene there where God's sort of divine counsel of angelic beings is there."],[1864.7,"It says they gathered on his right hand and on his left."],[1867.58,"And St. Gregory says those on the right hand are the elect angels."],[1871.5,"Those on his left hand are the angels who turn to wickedness."],[1876.38,"Right. Because uh the uh even these for St."],[1884.78,"Gregory and for St."],[1885.98,"Paul, even these angels that have rebelled are still being used by God sort of against their will."],[1893.5,"Right? God is inescapable."],[1897.02,"Right? God is God is all at all that they can't, you know, they can quote unquote rebel."],[1904.54,"They can hate him, but there's not like someplace they can go where he isn't."],[1910.06,"Right? There's not something, and so uh, as St."],[1914.14,"Gregory points out, as we see illustrated in the book of Job, right, with the the Satan there, right, they're sort of on a leash."],[1923.34,"Right? And so while they have malicious intent, God will use them, for example, to bring people to repentance."],[1929.66,"We talked about this in in 1 Corinthians when St."],[1932.06,"Paul talked about excommunicating someone and handing them over to Satan, and we're like, well, that's pretty harsh."],[1937.1,"But the idea was this would drive them to repentance."],[1942.02,"Right? That the sufferings inflicted, you know, the demon has nothing but malicious intent, but God is using what they're doing in order to bring people to repentance, to bring them, to bring them back to faith."],[1954.9,"Okay. So we're talking here about, or St."],[1959.22,"Paul is talking here about."],[1962.57,"His bringing of these Gentiles, these pagan nations, these members of these pagan nations to Christ."],[1969.77,"Okay. Well, if they're not with Christ."],[1976.01,"Christ is not their Lord."],[1978.01,"If they're, as Saint Paul was just saying, his imagery, if they're cut off."],[1982.01,"If they're outside the wall."],[1984.41,"The dividing wall."],[1986.57,"Who are they under?"],[1991.61,"They're under powers of principalities."],[1994.57,"Right? Right. They're under these rebellious spiritual powers."],[2000.65,"That accepted them."],[2001.53,"Right. Where they yeah, where they've been since since the Tower of Babel."],[2008.09,"Right? I'll run I'll run I'll run through this very quickly because I know I've run through it a bunch of times before."],[2013.37,"Um but um Deuteronomy 32 verse 8 says this is what happened at the Tower of Babel."],[2021.37,"When when the Most High divided the nations at the Tower of Babel, he divided them according to the number of the sons of God."],[2030.57,"Right, right. So he put these angelic beings over them."],[2035.05,"Right? They tried to draw draw God down in the Tower of Babel, right, to get him to do what they wanted to manipulate him, and he uh responded by distancing himself from his creation, putting them under the charge of uh lesser spiritual beings, these angelic powers."],[2062.25,"And then he we see that's that's Genesis 11, Genesis 12, he then comes to Abraham and draws near to him and starts again."],[2072.73,"Right? Um, so all of these nations are under, we've talked about this over like in 1 Corinthians what St."],[2080.65,"Paul says, right, what the what the nations offer in sacrifice, they offer to demons, as the Psalm says, all the gods of the nations are demons."],[2089.41,"So that's this idea."],[2090.93,"That's who they've been under, these powers and principalities."],[2094.45,"Okay. So when Saint Paul comes and preaches Christ."],[2101.73,"That preaching is twofold because what is what is the gospel."],[2107.97,"He's talking about preaching the gospel."],[2110.77,"The gospel is the victory of Christ."],[2113.33,"Right? He's proclaiming the victory of Christ."],[2115.73,"Over who? Over the angels."],[2118.85,"Over the over the devil, over the demons, over right the evil spiritual powers, over death itself."],[2126.21,"Over sin. That's what's being proclaimed."],[2130.45,"So that proclamation that St."],[2132.05,"Paul is making when he comes and preaches the gospel in Ephesus and in the area around Ephesus."],[2138.13,"Is sort of two parts depending on who hears it."],[2143.33,"So he's at once proclaiming to those spiritual powers who had formerly dominated these people, guess what?"],[2150.61,"You lost. Right?"],[2154.13,"Yeah, war's over, you're on the losing side."],[2158.29,"And proclaiming to the people who they had held captive now, hey, guess what?"],[2163.73,"They're defeated, the war's over, they lost, you're free."],[2167.89,"And it's Christ who set you free."],[2171.57,"So the gospel has both of those components."],[2175.81,"So that's what St."],[2177.33,"Paul is talking about here."],[2178.37,"This apostolic mission to come there and preach is to both."],[2182.37,"It's pronouncing doom."],[2184.77,"To those evil spiritual powers and freedom to those Gentiles."],[2190.25,"Those members, those pagans who had been enslaved to them at the same time when he comes and preaches God."],[2197.77,"So that mystery of who Christ is."],[2201.45,"As we have in our iconography."],[2203.53,"You see all the time, what looks like in English, I C XC."],[2207.37,"Which is it's actually a sigma, it's abbreviation for Jesus Christ, and then Nika conquers."],[2214.73,"Conqueror. So that's what Christ is, or that's what St."],[2218.41,"Paul is proclaiming Christ as."],[2220.81,"That's that's the mystery."],[2222.49,"Mystery is Christ himself."],[2225.53,"That's doom to them."],[2228.41,"And freedom to the people."],[2230.81,"So that's what St."],[2231.69,"Paul's talking about here when he talks about proclaiming the gospel to the powers and principalities of the heavenly places."],[2240.33,"Right? That's not."],[2241.93,"But remember, the gospel is not what you've got to do to get saved."],[2248.01,"Right? The book of Acts, when someone preaches the gospel, the people respond by saying, What must I do to be saved?"],[2256.57,"Right? Right. So if he had if if they just told him what they need to do to be saved, that would be a dumb question."],[2264.01,"Right? It would be like, wait, did I gotta repeat myself?"],[2267.37,"Right? So that's not what they proclaimed."],[2268.97,"They proclaimed who Christ is and what he'd done, the victory he'd won, that all authority in heaven on earth now belongs to him and not to these other powers, that he's gonna return to judge the living and the dead."],[2280.57,"And then after they heard that, they'd say, okay, what do I need to do?"],[2284.17,"Right then before he returns, to get myself right."],[2290.25,"And today's modern age, that's sort of a far-fetched idea."],[2297.41,"Which like all about like demons control the nations."],[2302.45,"Yeah. Like if we go out to the street and some random guy, hey, would Jesus conquered all these, you know, demons and stuff, you'd be like, what?"],[2311.41,"How would I proclaim the gospel today, I guess is what I'm asking."],[2314.05,"Like to an average person."],[2319.01,"Well, you talk about who Christ is and and what he's done."],[2322.61,"Right? I mean, if they don't believe in angels and demons, they're not going to believe in Jesus either, or God or that's not necessarily so."],[2331.89,"I think people today a lot of people, even people who think of themselves as Christians, would dismiss demons and angels and say, I believe in God."],[2345.57,"Right. Right. And I believe in Christ, then they may not mean the right thing when they say that, but angels and demons, no, no, no, no, that's that's superstition."],[2355.73,"They've got, yeah, they've got kind of a lowest common denominator version of Christianity."],[2360.29,"And depending on, I mean, it could get pretty low."],[2362.77,"It could be just sort of Jesus was a nice guy and said good things about how to live your life and love God."],[2369.65,"Yeah. You know, kind of thing."],[2371.01,"I mean, you could get down to that level."],[2372.85,"Oh, yeah, I know."],[2373.89,"Yeah. Right. But um."],[2381.81,"Yeah, what we have to, if we're if we're really preaching the gospel, right, we have to preach the actual gospel."],[2390.21,"Right? Who Christ actually is and what he actually did."],[2392.93,"Right. Right. Lots of people laughed at St."],[2395.01,"Paul, too. Right?"],[2396.69,"The Athenian philosophers all laughed at St."],[2397.33,"Paul when he started talking about the bodily resurrection because they thought that was absurd."],[2402.97,"Right? And so we sort of can't be can't, number one, we can't be scared of that."],[2408.33,"Right? It's a lot of times when we talk about preaching the gospel, we're still thinking of it in fundamentally Protestant terms."],[2417.05,"Right? Where it's my goal is to go and say something, give an elevator speech."],[2422.65,"Make it as pithy as I can that will bring this person to a crisis point where they make some kind of decision to be a Christian."],[2429.93,"Right? And that's not how the gospel works."],[2435.93,"Right? I mean, that's not how it works for St."],[2438.09,"Paul. St. Paul isn't just going around trying to get people to make a decision for Christ."],[2442.89,"How's it different?"],[2444.25,"Right? I don't understand where the fundamental difference is."],[2448.33,"I mean. Well, everything St."],[2450.09,"Paul is doing is talking about them becoming part of the church and having this destiny and continuing to work out their salvation with fear and trembling."],[2457.93,"Right? So it's not a single crisis point."],[2460.41,"Oh, okay. Yeah."],[2461.61,"Right? It's a transformation of their whole way of life."],[2465.05,"Right? Their whole culture."],[2466.81,"Right? Because they didn't have see, we, again, unlike ancient people, we have like this religion category over here."],[2474.33,"We got the religion box and the politics box and the my occupation and right, my relationships with my family and my feelings about this and you know, the TV I like to watch and my favorite movies."],[2488.65,"In these different boxes, right, that aren't integrated."],[2493.21,"And so for these pagans who St."],[2495.85,"Paul comes to, changing their quote unquote religion, is not going from worshiping this god to going and worshiping that god."],[2502.25,"And everything else about their life stays the same."],[2507.73,"Right? This changes what they eat and when."],[2510.45,"This changes, you know, what occupation they can hold."],[2514.85,"Right? They may have to quit the leave their job because the craftsman's guild is making pagan sacrifices."],[2520.69,"Right. Yes. Yeah."],[2524.21,"You know, the public feasts."],[2526.13,"They're probably going to be ostracized by their family."],[2529.01,"Right? I mean, this is a complete, you're now leaving your culture, your community, everything, and joining this other one."],[2538.77,"Right? And that's that's not a decision you just make one time and then go about your business and try not to be as sinful as you were before."],[2547.33,"Right. But it is still a decision."],[2550.29,"It's a thousand decisions."],[2554.37,"Right? Here's what I would compare it to."],[2557.33,"Right? Yes, when you decide to ask someone to marry you, you're asking them to make a decision at one point."],[2567.73,"Okay. But a marriage is not a single decision at one time."],[2574.05,"Right? It's a thousand decisions that both spouses have to continue to make from little tiny things to great big things."],[2586.37,"For the rest of their lives, if the marriage is going to continue, right, and thrive and be healthy and be wonderful."],[2594.13,"Same kind of idea."],[2596.25,"Right? Where a lot of times in the in the Protestant way of thinking, it becomes focused on making the proposal and having the proposal be accepted."],[2607.25,"It's sort of like focusing on the wedding rather than the marriage."],[2608.41,"Right? Sort of like focusing, yes."],[2611.05,"Right. Right? Which is also something we do all too often in our culture."],[2620.41,"Focus on the wedding rather than the marriage."],[2622.33,"The wedding is over in an hour."],[2624.97,"The marriage hopefully lasts a lot longer than that."],[2628.73,"So yeah, it's the same, it's the same kind of idea."],[2632.41,"Right? St. Paul isn't after, you know, just racking up the conversions."],[2638.01,"I did this many baptisms."],[2641.05,"Right? He's after successful marriages that last a lifetime for all of these people."],[2647.69,"That's why he keeps writing to them."],[2650.25,"He didn't just come to town, baptize a bunch of them, and then move on to the next town to make more converts."],[2657.53,"Right? But he's stayed with them and lived with them and shared their lives with them."],[2662.41,"And he writes to them after he leaves when he hears they're having problems."],[2665.93,"Right? So it's this ongoing, this ongoing thing."],[2671.05,"So all that is to say, right, when you ask about, well, how do I preach the gospel to somebody?"],[2677.61,"Right? It's more than just I need you to agree that this series of statements is true, and now you're a Christian, or now you're an Orthodox Christian."],[2693.05,"Right? It would make it a lot easier on you guys who are catechumans if that's that's all you had to do, if I could just give you a list of a truefalse test and you just had to pass it."],[2702.49,"Yeah. Right? Yeah, I agree with that."],[2704.89,"I agree with that."],[2706.33,"Yeah. Yeah. Um, but that's not how we do it in the Orthodox Church."],[2712.85,"Right? You got to spend a year, you know, getting into the practice and the flow of living an Orthodox life."],[2720.77,"You know, sometimes more than a year."],[2723.97,"Right? And that's see, even that has gotten a little off kilter in our modern American world because a lot of places catechesis has come become about teaching."],[2736.77,"Yeah. Right? Where it's like, oh, you want to join the Orthodox Church?"],[2740.21,"Okay, I'm gonna give you this class and I'm gonna teach you all this stuff about the seven ecumenical councils and stuff."],[2745.17,"That by the way, none of the crater Orthodox people in the church know."],[2748.77,"And uh then once I think you've mastered all of it, I'll chrismate you."],[2753.57,"Yeah. Right? And that's skewed."],[2756.85,"Right? Because in in the early church, catechesis took between one and three years."],[2762.21,"And it wasn't based on what you knew."],[2765.09,"It was based on your life."],[2769.41,"How sinful your life was, how far off track your life was."],[2774.61,"You would spend between one and three years repenting."],[2779.33,"Changing. Acclimating yourself to living a Christian life as opposed to the life you had been living before."],[2786.13,"Right? That's what it was about."],[2788.77,"Right. And of course, learning is part of that."],[2792.29,"And hopefully you're gonna continue to learn the rest of your life as a Christian."],[2795.49,"You're not gonna stop at some point think, okay, I got I got this whole uh Orthodox Christianity thing down, you know."],[2803.17,"Um but it's just a part of it."],[2806.93,"It's not about mastering some content or agreeing to some propositions, it's about learning a way of life."],[2813.81,"And you can't teach someone a way of life in an elevator conversation."],[2817.25,"Right. Yeah. You can't if you're talking to someone who's a materialist."],[2826.73,"Even if they're a materialist who is kind of bracketed off, okay, well, yeah, I think there's probably a God."],[2832.01,"Even if they consider themselves a Christian and say, you know, there's God and Jesus, I don't believe in all that other stuff."],[2837.69,"Right? Even if they've got those bracketed off, you're not going to get them to see the world in a whole different way."],[2844.41,"You know, at least I'm not."],[2845.93,"I don't know."],[2846.65,"Maybe you're super gifted with."],[2851.05,"And I would think if you pulled that off, it would be more by reading them a poem than by uh giving them some kind of prosaic um kind of uh logical argument or explanation."],[2865.45,"Um but you you're really not gonna change someone's whole view of the world and existence and life and the cosmos in five minutes."],[2873.37,"Yeah, no. It's not gonna happen."],[2877.85,"Right? And so that means uh we have to invest a lot more time in people, a lot more love and care and time and attention in people rather than just trying to sell them a fire insurance policy so they go to heaven and say to hell when they die, and saying, okay, good enough."],[2895.93,"Right, on to the next one."],[2900.01,"Um, but but see, for that, for these people who St."],[2909.05,"Paul is writing to, they would have had had that argument."],[2912.73,"They knew very well what he was talking about."],[2915.05,"They were very familiar with these spirits they'd been worshiping."],[2918.41,"Right. They had oracles and seers and stuff who are possessed by these spirits and spoke that right."],[2924.05,"I mean, this was a very real thing for them."],[2927.81,"Right. And their whole lives have been governed."],[2932.21,"I mean, especially Greco-Roman religion is incredibly fatalistic."],[2937.49,"Right? Your destiny is not in your own hands, it's in the hands of these spiritual beings who you're constantly trying to sort of appease and do all the right rituals and motions so they'll be happy with you and let you keep going."],[2950.93,"Right? So that sense of slavery and bondage was very real for them, too."],[2956.05,"So when St."],[2956.77,"Paul says you're free from this."],[2959.81,"Christ has set you free from this and free from death."],[2963.97,"Right, which is the biggest threat that anyone could hold over your head."],[2969.09,"Right. And if you're a woman or a slave, by the way, Christ loves you just as much as that freeman over there."],[2976.77,"Right? This is a powerful thing that they experienced sort of immediately."],[2983.41,"Right. We, as modern sort of materialistic people, are less aware of the spiritual bondage we're in."],[2990.93,"That doesn't make it any less real."],[2993.57,"There are plenty of atheists out there addicted to pornography, addicted to drugs and addicted to alcohol, who are under the sway of sinful passions, addicted to anger, pride, whatever."],[3007.01,"Right. They don't acknowledge that there's any spiritual dimension to that."],[3012.85,"Right? But that doesn't mean there isn't."],[3014.77,"That doesn't mean they're not really in bondage."],[3017.81,"And don't really need to be set free from it."],[3021.17,"It's just we're not used to thinking of it in those in those spiritual terms."]],"o":[{"t":23.66,"lv":2,"h":"Recap: Ephesians 1-2","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Ephesians = probably written <b>from Ephesus, not to Ephesus</b> - circulated around Ephesus, <b>Asia Minor</b> (now Turkey)</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Chapter 1</b>: laying out <b>theosis</b></li><li class=\"d1\">destiny of humans: <b>adopted as sons of God</b>, share God's <b>eternal divine life</b></li><li class=\"d0\">End of <b>chapter 2</b>: segue from renewal of humanity in Christ → <b>unity of Jews and Gentiles</b></li><li class=\"d1\">pagan or Judean, now in Christ = <b>new creation</b>, same <b>new humanity</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Ended with <b>temple</b> metaphor</li><li class=\"d1\">foundation laid by <b>apostles and prophets</b>, Christ the <b>chief cornerstone</b></li><li class=\"d1\">us as <b>living bricks</b> - place where God dwells among them</li><li class=\"d0\">\"Quickest recap I've ever done\"; \"unless anyone has really late election results\"</li></ul>"},{"t":171.1,"lv":2,"h":"3:1 - Prisoner of Christ Jesus","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">\"For this reason, I, Paul, the <b>prisoner of Christ Jesus</b>, for you Gentiles. If indeed you have heard of the <b>dispensation of the grace of God</b>, which was given to me for you\"</li><li class=\"d0\">One of Paul's <b>very, very long sentences</b> - \"even in English\"</li><li class=\"d1\">\"truly a St. Paul Greek sentence\" when they can't figure out where to break it - <b>nested and complex</b></li><li class=\"d0\">\"For this reason\" = everything just recapped</li><li class=\"d0\">Prisoner is <b>literal</b> - in jail</li><li class=\"d1\">his time in Ephesus \"somewhat troubled\" in <b>Acts</b>; \"in prison many times\"</li></ul>"},{"t":259.74,"lv":3,"h":"\"Prisoner of\" - genitive","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>Committee translations</b> \"punt\" - give the most <b>bare-bones non-committal</b> wording</li><li class=\"d1\">\"prisoner of Christ\" sounds like <b>Christ has him in a cage</b></li><li class=\"d0\">No preposition in Greek - just a <b>genitive</b>; interpreted various ways</li><li class=\"d1\">\"a prisoner <b>related to</b> Christ Jesus\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Paul's point: <b>not a prisoner of the people who imprisoned him</b></li><li class=\"d1\">not a crime; <b>not complaining about persecution</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Two reasons he's in prison</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>for Christ</b> - belongs to Christ</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>for the sake of the Gentiles</b> - former pagans now in the church</li></ul>"},{"t":395.9,"lv":3,"h":"3:2 - Dispensation of the grace of God","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">\"If indeed you have heard of the <b>dispensation of the grace of God</b>, given to me for you\"</li><li class=\"d1\">= the last two chapters: gift of salvation, <b>adoption and sonship</b></li><li class=\"d0\">\"If you heard about it from me\" → \"I'm locked up because I came <b>preaching this for you</b>\"</li><li class=\"d1\">promoting the cause of Christ, proclaiming grace to former pagans</li><li class=\"d1\">not an actual crime, not \"the governor hates him personally\"</li></ul>"},{"t":477.7,"lv":2,"h":"3:3 - By revelation, the mystery","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">\"<b>By revelation</b> he made known to me the <b>mystery</b>, as I have <b>briefly written already</b>, by which when you read you may understand my knowledge in the mystery of Christ\"</li><li class=\"d0\">\"How that\" → more detail on the dispensation: \"here's what I mean by that\"</li><li class=\"d0\">\"Briefly written already\" - previous letter we don't have?</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>ambiguous</b> - could be the last two chapters, or another communication</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Revelation</b> = Christ revealed himself to Paul on the <b>road to Damascus</b>, made known the mystery</li><li class=\"d1\">Christ gives knowledge of the mystery → Paul conveys it to them</li></ul>"},{"t":604.22,"lv":2,"h":"What \"mystery\" meant","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Not \"mystery like <b>who done it</b>\"; not \"purely <b>esoteric</b>\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Modern ear: a <b>secret fact</b> kept hidden, then conveyed to Paul</li><li class=\"d1\">not what mystery meant in <b>first-century Ephesus</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Mystery cults</b> (cf. intro to <b>1 Corinthians</b>, <b>Demeter</b> in Corinth)</li><li class=\"d1\">not like <b>Scientology</b> - level reached, told about \"Dark Lord <b>Xenu</b>, aliens, volcanoes\"</li><li class=\"d1\">not secret stuff like the <b>Freemasons</b></li><li class=\"d0\">What made them mystery cults: <b>rites of initiation</b></li><li class=\"d1\">not factual information - <b>extreme experiences</b>, like \"hazing on the way to a fraternity... much more extreme\"</li><li class=\"d1\">most involved <b>death, near death, entering the realm of the dead</b>; spiritual death and rebirth</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>Persephone</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Examples: darkness, edges of <b>pits and cliffs</b>, falling; under a grate while a <b>bull's blood</b> is dumped on you; <b>psychedelic drugs</b></li><li class=\"d1\">afterward: a <b>religious experience</b> of death and rebirth → new perspective on the world</li><li class=\"d0\">Q: weren't they promising <b>eternal life</b>? \"Eventually down the road, yeah\"</li></ul>"},{"t":845.82,"lv":3,"h":"Christ himself is the mystery","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>Chapter 2</b>: deification - not <b>apotheosis</b> where you do mighty deeds to impress the gods</li><li class=\"d0\">Similar idea here: Paul describes an <b>experience on the road to Damascus</b></li><li class=\"d1\">Christ <b>revealed himself</b> - didn't tell him arcane secrets</li><li class=\"d1\">no <b>secret name of God</b> to make magic happen</li><li class=\"d1\">no keywords to get past <b>gatekeepers to the afterlife</b> - \"like in <b>Isis</b> cults\"</li><li class=\"d0\">\"Christ Himself who is the mystery\"</li><li class=\"d1\">tied to <b>John's Gospel</b>: Christ as the <b>logos</b>, the reason behind creation</li><li class=\"d1\">in Christ → \"look out and make sense of the world\"; adoption and <b>eternal life</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Not esoteric - not pilgrimage and rituals; <b>coming to know Christ</b></li><li class=\"d1\">not imposed by another person; <b>no technique, magic, smoke and mirrors, chemicals, blood of a bull</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Paul reveals Christ to the Ephesian pagans</li><li class=\"d1\">adoption <b>plus</b> the means to understand <b>world, life, cosmos</b></li><li class=\"d1\">no need to search for \"other cosmic mysteries\"</li></ul>"},{"t":1043.34,"lv":2,"h":"Q&amp;A: Paul's words vs direct experience","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Q: \"provocative\" - Paul had direct experience; how does <b>hearing him</b> do the same?</li><li class=\"d0\">They're now <b>in Christ</b> through <b>baptism</b> - \"come to know Christ <b>themselves</b>, not just heard about him\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Why this wording: former pagans' view of religion, <b>and</b> not a \"philosophical system or self-help system\"</li><li class=\"d1\">\"not like <b>stoicism</b>, here's how to have a happy and successful life\"</li><li class=\"d1\">coming to know <b>Christ Himself</b> - \"that's the grace of God\" (ch. 1-2)</li><li class=\"d0\">Paul's proclamation = <b>means by which Christ chooses to reveal himself</b></li><li class=\"d1\">\"It's not his preaching that does it\"</li></ul>"},{"t":1163.46,"lv":3,"h":"Like prayer: not magic","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Same as <b>prayer</b>: not magic that <b>makes God do something</b></li><li class=\"d1\">\"enough people, the right people... then God will do what we want\" - <b>not how it works</b></li><li class=\"d1\">God <b>chooses to work through</b> the prayers of the saints</li><li class=\"d0\">Paul preached in many places - <b>not everybody</b> had direct experience</li><li class=\"d1\">people laughed, some threw him in jail</li><li class=\"d1\">even those who met Christ in person didn't all \"meet\" him in this sense</li><li class=\"d0\">\"Not magic\" - the means by which Paul has been <b>called to bring Christ to the pagan nations</b></li><li class=\"d1\">his life \"sort of a <b>prayer</b>\" offered to God to use \"as God sees fit. Not as Paul sees fit\"</li></ul>"},{"t":1256.3,"lv":2,"h":"3:5 - Revealed by the Spirit","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">\"Which in other ages was not made known to the <b>sons of men</b>, as it has now been revealed by the Spirit to his holy <b>apostles and prophets</b>\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Not <b>theology-book content</b> - \"they had no idea who Jesus was back then\" is wrong; \"the opposite\" all through the Gospels</li><li class=\"d1\">\"<b>Abraham</b> rejoiced to see one of my days\"</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>Transfiguration</b> on Tabor: Moses and Elijah aren't \"who are you?\" - Moses talked to him on <b>Sinai</b></li><li class=\"d0\">What wasn't known: Christ himself to <b>everybody</b></li><li class=\"d1\"><b>average Israelite</b> never had a direct encounter - not face to face</li><li class=\"d1\">prophets did: <b>Moses, Elijah, Isaiah, Jeremiah, Abraham</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Transition: Christ's death, resurrection, ascension, <b>Pentecost</b> - Spirit comes upon <b>all flesh</b></li><li class=\"d1\">OT: Spirit on <b>David, Moses, prophets</b> - \"your average Israelite, no\"</li><li class=\"d1\">often <b>not permanent</b>: Spirit on <b>Saul</b>, Saul sins, Spirit leaves</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>Judges</b>: Spirit falls on a judge for a period, then leaves</li><li class=\"d0\">Now the province of <b>everyone</b> - including former pagan Gentiles</li><li class=\"d1\">through the <b>apostles</b>: Spirit first on them at Pentecost → preach → hearers <b>baptized, receive the Spirit</b></li></ul>"},{"t":1480.14,"lv":2,"h":"3:6 - Fellow heirs, same body","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">\"That the Gentiles should be <b>fellow heirs</b> of the <b>same body</b> and <b>partakers of his promise</b> in Christ through the gospel\"</li><li class=\"d0\">All pagan nations fellow heirs <b>along with Judah</b></li><li class=\"d0\">That's the goal: <b>call everybody back in</b></li><li class=\"d1\">they didn't have direct access before</li><li class=\"d1\">= <b>Paul's mission</b></li></ul>"},{"t":1529.3,"lv":2,"h":"3:7 - Minister by God's working","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">\"Of which I became a <b>minister</b> according to the <b>gift of the grace of God</b>... by the <b>effective working of his power</b>\" - \"no sentence break yet in this chapter\"</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>God's action</b> - took him, made him an apostle, sent him</li><li class=\"d1\">not something Paul <b>attained</b>; didn't meditate</li><li class=\"d1\">not initiated into some mystery; didn't go to <b>Jerusalem</b> to be initiated by the other apostles</li><li class=\"d1\">\"God <b>grabbed him</b> on the road to Damascus\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Emphasis: Paul's there doing it, but really <b>God doing it for them through Paul</b></li></ul>"},{"t":1628.58,"lv":2,"h":"3:8 - Less than the least","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">\"To me, who am <b>less than the least of all the saints</b>, this grace was given that I should preach among the nations the <b>unsearchable riches of Christ</b>\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Saints = <b>holy ones, sons of God</b> - he's the <b>least</b> of them</li><li class=\"d1\">despite that, God gave him the gift to preach to <b>all the nations</b></li></ul>"},{"t":1676.86,"lv":2,"h":"3:9 - The mystery hidden in God","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">\"Make all see what is the <b>fellowship of the mystery</b>, which from the beginning of the ages has been <b>hidden in God</b>, who created all things through Jesus Christ\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Not a mystery <b>still hidden</b> that you go through rituals to have revealed</li><li class=\"d1\">Paul <b>proclaiming it to everyone</b> - Christ</li><li class=\"d0\">Christ <b>hidden in the past</b>, even though <b>through him</b> the Father created everything</li><li class=\"d1\">didn't \"come into being recently\" - there the whole time</li><li class=\"d1\">revealed to everyone <b>recently</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Not saying nobody knew him - prophets did - but <b>not known to everyone</b></li><li class=\"d1\">now pagan nations hear who he is through the <b>apostles</b></li></ul>"},{"t":1766.34,"lv":2,"h":"3:10 - Wisdom made known to the powers","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">\"To the intent that now the <b>manifold wisdom of God</b> might be made known by the <b>church</b> to the <b>principalities and powers in the heavenly places</b> according to the eternal purpose accomplished in Christ\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Who? <b>Powers and principalities</b> in the heavenly places - \"we do not battle against flesh and blood\" (will get there)</li><li class=\"d0\">Not \"all thrown out of the heavenly places\" - Paul doesn't talk that way</li><li class=\"d1\">our war is with powers <b>in the heavenly places</b></li></ul>"},{"t":1844.78,"lv":3,"h":"Gregory: angels on a leash","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>St. Gregory the Dialogist</b>, <i>Moralia</i> (commentary on <b>Job</b>)</li><li class=\"d1\">divine council: gathered on his <b>right hand and left</b></li><li class=\"d1\">right = <b>elect angels</b>; left = angels who <b>turned to wickedness</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Even rebel angels <b>used by God against their will</b></li><li class=\"d1\">\"<b>God is inescapable</b>\" - they can hate him, nowhere to go where he isn't</li><li class=\"d1\">\"on a <b>leash</b>\" - <b>the Satan</b> in Job</li><li class=\"d0\">God uses them to bring people to <b>repentance</b></li><li class=\"d1\"><b>1 Corinthians</b>: excommunicating, handing over to Satan - \"pretty harsh\" - drives to repentance</li><li class=\"d1\">demon has only <b>malicious intent</b>; God uses it to bring them back to faith</li></ul>"},{"t":1954.9,"lv":2,"h":"Gentiles under the powers since Babel","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Paul brings pagan nations to Christ - if not with Christ, <b>who are they under</b>?</li><li class=\"d1\">outside the <b>dividing wall</b> → under <b>rebellious spiritual powers</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Since the <b>Tower of Babel</b> - <b>Deuteronomy 32:8</b></li><li class=\"d1\">Most High divided the nations \"according to the number of the <b>sons of God</b>\"</li><li class=\"d1\">angelic beings put over them</li><li class=\"d0\">Babel: tried to <b>draw God down</b>, manipulate him → he <b>distanced himself</b>, put nations under <b>lesser spiritual beings</b></li><li class=\"d1\"><b>Genesis 11 → 12</b>: draws near to <b>Abraham</b>, starts again</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>1 Corinthians</b>: what nations offer in sacrifice they offer to <b>demons</b>; Psalm: \"all the gods of the nations are <b>demons</b>\"</li></ul>"},{"t":2094.45,"lv":2,"h":"Gospel: doom to the powers, freedom to the people","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Preaching is <b>twofold</b></li><li class=\"d1\">gospel = <b>the victory of Christ</b> - over <b>angels, devil, demons, evil powers, death, sin</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Depending on who hears it</li><li class=\"d1\">to the powers who dominated these people: \"<b>you lost</b>. War's over, you're on the losing side\"</li><li class=\"d1\">to captives: \"they're defeated, the war's over, <b>you're free</b>. It's Christ who set you free\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Apostolic mission = <b>doom</b> to evil powers, <b>freedom</b> to Gentiles</li><li class=\"d0\">Iconography: <b>IC XC NIKA</b> - Jesus Christ <b>conquers</b> (sigma = abbreviation)</li><li class=\"d1\">\"Mystery is Christ himself\" - doom to them, freedom to the people</li></ul>"},{"t":2241.93,"lv":3,"h":"The gospel is not \"what you've got to do\"","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>Acts</b>: hearers respond \"<b>What must I do to be saved?</b>\"</li><li class=\"d1\">if told what to do, it'd be a dumb question - \"did I gotta repeat myself?\"</li><li class=\"d0\">What they proclaimed: <b>who Christ is</b>, what he'd done</li><li class=\"d1\">victory won; <b>all authority</b> in heaven and earth his, not the other powers'</li><li class=\"d1\">he'll <b>return to judge</b> the living and the dead</li><li class=\"d1\">then: \"what do I need to do before he returns?\"</li></ul>"},{"t":2290.25,"lv":2,"h":"Q&amp;A: proclaiming the gospel today","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Q: far-fetched today - \"demons control the nations\" - how would I proclaim to an average person?</li><li class=\"d0\">Talk about <b>who Christ is and what he's done</b></li><li class=\"d1\">many \"Christians\" dismiss angels and demons: \"I believe in God... <b>superstition</b>\"</li><li class=\"d1\">\"lowest common denominator\" - Jesus was a <b>nice guy</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Preach the <b>actual gospel</b> - who Christ <b>actually</b> is, what he <b>actually</b> did</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>Athenian philosophers</b> laughed at Paul over <b>bodily resurrection</b> - \"can't be scared of that\"</li><li class=\"d0\">We think in <b>Protestant terms</b>: <b>elevator speech</b>, pithy, bring someone to a <b>crisis point</b> and a decision</li><li class=\"d1\">not how it works for Paul - not \"decision for Christ\"</li></ul>"},{"t":2444.25,"lv":3,"h":"Q&amp;A: how is that different? Whole way of life","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Q: where's the fundamental difference?</li><li class=\"d0\">Paul's concern: becoming part of the church, destiny, \"<b>work out salvation with fear and trembling</b>\"</li><li class=\"d1\">not a single crisis point - <b>transformation of whole way of life, whole culture</b></li><li class=\"d0\">We have boxes: <b>religion, politics, occupation, family, TV</b> - \"not integrated\"</li><li class=\"d1\">for pagans, changing religion ≠ swapping gods and keeping everything else</li><li class=\"d1\">changes <b>what they eat and when</b>; <b>occupation</b> (craftsman's guild pagan sacrifices); public feasts</li><li class=\"d1\">likely <b>ostracized by family</b> - leaving culture, community</li><li class=\"d0\">\"Not a decision you make one time\" - \"but it is still a decision. It's a <b>thousand decisions</b>\"</li></ul>"},{"t":2554.37,"lv":3,"h":"Marriage, not wedding","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>Proposal</b> = one decision; a <b>marriage</b> = a thousand decisions by both spouses, small and great, for life</li><li class=\"d0\">Protestant focus on the <b>proposal being accepted</b> = \"focusing on the <b>wedding</b> rather than the marriage\"</li><li class=\"d1\">\"wedding over in an hour\"; marriage lasts longer - also our culture</li><li class=\"d0\">Paul not \"racking up conversions\", \"I did this many baptisms\"</li><li class=\"d1\">after <b>successful marriages that last a lifetime</b></li><li class=\"d1\">stays with them, lives with them; <b>writes after he leaves</b> when he hears of problems</li></ul>"},{"t":2671.05,"lv":2,"h":"Catechesis as a way of life","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">\"How do I preach the gospel?\" - more than agreeing a <b>series of statements is true</b></li><li class=\"d1\">easier for catechumens with a <b>true/false test</b> - \"not how we do it\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Orthodox: a year or more in the <b>practice and flow</b> of an Orthodox life</li><li class=\"d1\">modern America: catechesis = <b>teaching</b>; class on seven ecumenical councils \"none of the cradle Orthodox know\", then chrismate - \"skewed\"</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Early church</b>: catechesis <b>one to three years</b></li><li class=\"d1\">based on your <b>life</b>, not what you knew - how sinful, how far off track</li><li class=\"d1\">spend it <b>repenting, changing</b>, acclimating to a Christian life</li><li class=\"d1\">learning part of it, lifelong - but \"learning a <b>way of life</b>\"</li><li class=\"d0\">\"You can't teach a way of life in an <b>elevator conversation</b>\"</li><li class=\"d1\">materialist, or \"Jesus but not all that other stuff\" - not changed in five minutes</li><li class=\"d1\">more by \"reading them a <b>poem</b>\" than a logical argument</li><li class=\"d0\">→ invest <b>time, love, care, attention</b> - not \"selling a <b>fire insurance policy</b>... on to the next one\"</li></ul>"},{"t":2900.01,"lv":2,"h":"Bondage and freedom","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Ephesians' audience knew exactly what Paul meant</li><li class=\"d1\">familiar with <b>spirits they'd worshiped</b> - <b>oracles and seers</b> possessed and speaking</li><li class=\"d1\">Greco-Roman religion \"incredibly <b>fatalistic</b>\" - destiny in the hands of spiritual beings you appease with rituals</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>slavery and bondage</b> very real</li><li class=\"d0\">Paul: Christ set you free from this and from <b>death</b> - \"biggest threat anyone could hold over your head\"</li><li class=\"d1\">\"if you're a <b>woman or a slave</b>, Christ loves you just as much as that <b>freeman</b>\"</li><li class=\"d1\">experienced \"sort of immediately\"</li></ul>"},{"t":2983.41,"lv":3,"h":"Modern spiritual bondage","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">We \"modern, materialistic\" are less aware of it - <b>no less real</b></li><li class=\"d1\"><b>atheists</b> addicted to <b>pornography, drugs, alcohol</b>; under sway of passions - <b>anger, pride</b></li><li class=\"d1\">don't acknowledge a spiritual dimension - doesn't mean they're not in bondage, don't need to be <b>set free</b></li><li class=\"d1\">\"not used to thinking of it in those spiritual terms\"</li></ul>"}]});
